+### Validation record (iteration 1 — all items pass)
+
+- **Implementation details**: The field names (`burn_after_reading`, `password`, `protected`), the
+  header name (`X-Paste-Password`), and the status codes are protocol surface fixed by the request
+  and by the service that already exists — not design choices made by this spec. They are recorded
+  in the **Constraints** section exactly as `001-pastebin-service` records its own, and the user
+  stories, edge cases, and success criteria are written behaviourally. No language, framework,
+  library, module, file, or data-format decision appears. SR-013 names a *class* of algorithm
+  (salted, deliberately slow, purpose-built) rather than a specific one, which the constitution's
+  Security Baseline requires of every specification; choosing the algorithm is left to the plan.
+- **Technology-agnostic success criteria**: SC-020 and SC-021 refer to the automated test suite
+  because constitution Principle III makes requirement-to-test traceability itself a stated
+  requirement; this mirrors SC-008 of `001-pastebin-service`. All other criteria are stated as
+  caller-observable outcomes with 100%/0%/exactly-one targets.
